(4. Pre-Training: Next-Token Prediction at Scale) Tj
T*
(During pre-training, the model reads billions of pages of books, articles, and) Tj
T*
(open codebases. Its objective is remarkably simple: predict the next token) Tj
T*
(given all preceding tokens. By practicing this trillions of times, the model) Tj
T*
(internalizes grammar, world facts, reasoning patterns, and cause-and-effect.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Fine-Tuning and Instruction Following) Tj
T*
(A raw pre-trained model only predicts text continuations; it does not naturally) Tj
T*
(act as a helpful study partner. Supervised Fine-Tuning \(SFT\) teaches the model) Tj
T*
(using curated question-and-answer examples written by human experts. Afterward,) Tj
T*
(Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback \(RLHF\) scores multiple answers so) Tj
T*
(the model prefers accurate, concise, and safe responses over rambling guesses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Context Windows and Memory Limits) Tj
T*
(The context window is the maximum number of tokens a model can inspect in a) Tj
T*
(single request, including both your prompt and its reply. Modern models handle) Tj
T*
(hundreds of thousands of tokens, enough for full research papers. However, very) Tj
T*
(long inputs increase latency and cost, so chunking documents into focused) Tj
T*
(sections remains an essential engineering practice for fast, reliable tools.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
